     "category_en": "Commodities",
     "time": "09:52",
     "title_en": "the National Bureau of Statistics: High-tech manufacturing and equipment manufacturing PMIs in October were 51.3% and 50.6%, respectively.",
     "body_en": "the National Bureau of Statistics said that in October, the manufacturing PMI fell to 49.3% due to factors such as the early release of some demand before the 11/11 holiday and the complex and volatile international environment. New momentum keeps growing faster. The PMIs of the high-tech manufacturing industry and the equipment manufacturing industry were 51.3% and 50.6%, respectively, which continued to be higher than the critical point. The production and operation of enterprises in related industries maintained expansion, and the new quality productivity continued to develop well. The PMIs of the consumer goods industry and the energy-intensive industry were 48.8% and 47.3%, respectively, down 1.9 percentage points and 0.7 percentage points from the previous month, and market activity weakened.",
